Key Concepts Demonstrated

Spying on class methods - We spy on apiClient.fetchUser and apiClient.saveUser
Mock return values - Control what the API returns without making real calls
Verify call counts - Check how many times methods were called
Verify call arguments - Ensure methods were called with correct parameters
Test caching logic - Verify API is only called when cache misses
Mock errors - Test error handling with mockRejectedValueOnce
Sequential mocks - Different return values for consecutive calls

This pattern is perfect for testing code that depends on external services, databases, or any expensive operations!

