Spy vs Mock vs Spy + Mock

// 1. SPY ONLY (watches but doesn't change behavior)
const spy = jest.spyOn(apiClient, 'fetchUser');
// ✓ Tracks calls, arguments, return values
// ✗ Still makes real API call (not what we want for tests!)

// 2. MOCK ONLY (replaces function completely)
apiClient.fetchUser = jest.fn(() => Promise.resolve({ id: 1, name: 'John' }));
// ✓ No real API call
// ✗ Lost reference to original function, harder to restore

// 3. SPY + MOCK (best of both worlds - what we're doing)
const spy = jest.spyOn(apiClient, 'fetchUser')
  .mockImplementation(() => Promise.resolve({ id: 1, name: 'John' }));
// ✓ Tracks calls, arguments, return values
// ✓ No real API call
// ✓ Can easily restore with mockRestore()